{
 "title": "United in Currency, Divided in Growth: Dynamic Effects of Euro Adoption - Replication Spec",
 "hypothesis": "Euro adoption reduced annual real GDP per capita growth under conditional parallel trends",
 "data_sources": [
  "Penn World Tables 10.0 (rgdpe/pop, log diff growth, productivity, human capital)",
  "World Bank World Development Indicators (consumption, investment, net exports, additional macro indicators)"
 ],
 "sample": "Unbalanced country-year panel 35 countries 1970-2023. Treatment: 20 current eurozone members (11 founding 1999: Austria, Belgium, Finland, France, Germany, Ireland, Italy, Luxembourg, Netherlands, Portugal, Spain; 9 late: Greece 2001, Slovenia 2007, Cyprus 2008, Malta 2008, Slovakia 2009, Estonia 2011, Latvia 2014, Lithuania 2015, Croatia 2023). Control: 15 (3 EU opt-out Denmark, Sweden, UK until 2020 + 12 other OECD: Australia, Canada, Iceland, Israel, Japan, Korea, New Zealand, Norway, Switzerland, US). Heterogeneity features measured 1998 or year before adoption: initial GDP per capita 2017$, trade openness, investment share, human capital index, standardized. Event time k_it = t - T_i^euro. Main estimation window k in [-10,20] (figure k in [-5,20]), placebo/anticipation checks with fake dates 1995,1997 and alternative treatment 1995 Madrid summit. Exclude <10 years pre-treatment for late adopters in main, included in robustness.",
 "period_start": "1970",
 "period_end": "2023",
 "method": [
  "Step 1 - Variable construction: primary outcome annual real GDP per capita growth = log diff rgdpe/pop (expenditure-side, 2017 prices). Treatment D_it=1 if adopted euro by year t. Event time k_it defined for treated; never-treated controls k undefined/placeholder. Mechanism outcomes: consumption growth (household final consumption), investment growth (gross fixed capital formation), net exports %GDP, labor productivity growth (output per worker), TFP rtpfna.",
  "Step 2 - Features: X_i vector pre-treatment: initial GDP per capita, trade openness (%GDP), investment share (%GDP), human capital index. All continuous features standardized. Node-level residualization: within each tree node l compute Y~ - alpha_i^l - gamma_t^l and D~ - pi_i^l - rho_t^l (country+year FE estimated on observations in node l).",
  "Step 3 - Causal Forests with Fixed Effects (CFFE) using causalfe Python (Kattenberg R reference). Hyperparameters: param_n_trees_main = 500 trees, Minimum leaf size param_min_leaf_main = 30 observations, Honesty enabled (separate split/estimation subsamples), node-level FE residualization. Robustness varies trees 100/200/500, depth 3/5/7, leaf 20/30/50. Model: Y_it = alpha_i + gamma_t + tau(k_it,X_i)*D_it + epsilon_it.",
  "Step 4 - Dynamic ATT: tau_hat(k,X) learned forest nonparametrically. Average dynamic effect tau_hat(k)=1/N_k sum_{i:k_it=k} tau_hat(k,X_i). Cluster-robust variance: Var =1/N_k^2 sum_i (sum_{t:k_it=k} (tau_hat_it - tau_hat(k)))^2. Forest-based CI (Wager). Block bootstrap param_bootstrap_B=200 resamples entire country time series with replacement. Pre-treatment k<0 examined for placebo/parallel trends.",
  "Step 5 - Benchmark/comparisons: Classical TWFE event study Y_it=alpha_i+gamma_t+ sum_{k=-10}^{20} beta_k*1[k_it=k]+epsilon_it k=-1 reference clustered SE; Sun-Abraham (2021) interaction-weighted cohort aggregation; Callaway-Sant'Anna (2021) doubly-robust group-time ATT; Bai (2009) interactive FE Y_it=alpha_i+ lambda_i'f_t + tau D_it+epsilon_it. Alternative control EU-only (Denmark,Sweden,UK) vs OECD baseline; crisis separation excluding 2008-2015, pre-crisis k<9 vs k>=9; anticipation 1995/1997 treatment dates; sample restrictions founders-only/EU15/excl crisis countries/core-only.",
  "Step 6 - Mechanisms/heterogeneity: re-estimate CFFE with same structure for consumption, investment, net exports, productivity/TFP, current account. Feature importance = proportion of splits using variable. Country-level CATE tau_hat(k) trajectories and counterfactual predictions for non-euro EU members (UK, Sweden, Denmark) had they adopted 1999. Correlation with Gabriel et al SCM estimates. DSGE two-country NK with hysteresis (sequence-space Jacobian): IS, NKPC, scarring a_H=rho_a a_H-1+chi x_H-1+eps, Taylor union i=rho_i i_-1+(1-rho_i)(phi_pi pi^EA+phi_x x^EA) vs float country Taylor, UIP and q dynamics; calibration table DSGE."
 ],
